# ── Binaries & build artifacts ──────────────────────────────
/caddy
/caddy.exe
*.tar.gz

# ── Logs & runtime output ───────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
api-out.log
api-err.log
healthcheck.out.log
prism.out.log

# ── Caddy runtime state ─────────────────────────────────────
autosave.json

# ── Editor / OS cruft ───────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/

# ── Python bytecode ─────────────────────────────────────────
# F21 made api-server.py import a sibling module (extract.py), so running the
# server now writes __pycache__/ next to the source. Those are build artifacts
# and must never reach the repo.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.idea/

# ── Playwright / debug residue ──────────────────────────────
.playwright-mcp/

# ── Local secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.credentials

# NOTE: scripts/lib/fake-key.pem IS committed, on purpose. It is a throwaway
# self-signed key for a localhost test double, with no production use, and
# committing it is what lets the TLS suites run on a fresh checkout with no
# /tmp state. A generic *.pem ignore here would silently break F22/F24/F25/F26
# on every other machine, which is the exact failure this file is fixing.
